WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.792
This query reads the patient-admission summary view.

00:00:02.792 --> 00:00:06.987
Consumers do not need to repeat the join or stay-duration expression.

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:09.527
The view already defines that interface.

00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:11.562
Run it and identify the grain.

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:17.047
One row represents one admission with selected patient attributes and a derived stay duration.

00:00:17.047 --> 00:00:21.547
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:27.147
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:29.377
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:29.377 --> 00:00:35.357
In a real setting such as a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption,

00:00:35.357 --> 00:00:40.862
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:42.922
before discussing syntax.

00:00:42.922 --> 00:00:48.560
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
